/looper
.code-analysis/

# CI checks the parity oracle (narthur/skills, for internal/record's parity gate) out
# here. It must be IGNORED, not merely untracked: `git status --porcelain` lists
# untracked paths, so the mutation-score step's clean-tree guard aborted on it.
.parity-oracle/
# CI writes the verbose record-package test output here so the next step can assert the
# parity gate did not skip. Ignored for the same reason as above: the mutation-score step
# runs afterwards and its clean-tree guard counts untracked paths.
record.log
# The same, for the push package's oracle step — and it was MISSED when that step was added,
# which meant the mutation-score step could never run at all: `?? push.log` made
# requireCleanTree abort with "refusing to run: 1 uncommitted change(s)", a message about
# uncommitted work rather than about a log file. Every raise of the catalog floor since was
# gating on a step that aborted. Nothing caught it because this branch has not reached CI yet,
# so the lesson is the pairing: a step that writes a log into the workspace needs a line here
# in the same commit.
push.log
